{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "version": 2,
  "description": "Standardized navigation phrase corpus for TTS engine benchmarking. Each phrase has a stable ID. Language codes: ne (Nepali), en (English), ne-en (mixed). 'text' is the exact phrase to synthesize; 'display_text' is an optional human-readable form for mixed phrases (TTS engines may not accept Devanagari script, so the tts_text field is provided where a Latin-script rendering is required).",
  "metadata_notes": {
    "tts_text": "Latin-script rendering of the phrase, for engines that cannot process Devanagari script (e.g. some English-only models). null when the original text is already Latin script.",
    "expected_pronunciation": "Informal pronunciation guidance for the Nepali portions. Benchmark example material, not final product copy.",
    "review_status": "Content review status: 'draft', 'needs-review', or 'approved'. Rewritten phrases are initially 'needs-review' — native-speaker review is required before the corpus is considered final.",
    "content_principles": "Nepali phrases are authored as native conversational Nepali (not literal translations of English). Borrowed English-origin words (स्पिड, क्यामेरा, ट्राफिक, पुलिस) are written in Devanagari when that is what a Nepali speaker would naturally say. Personality modifies wording/delivery while preserving navigation meaning."
  },
